# Calibration test templates

## Canonical source

`tester-v1/calibration-tests/` is the only source for shared probe YAML. The create-model-configs skill copies bench YAML from here, never from live model dirs.

**In calibration-tests:** global probes for calibration (`calibration-footprint`, `calibration-ctx-probe`, `hello-world-baseline`, plus any future promoted probes).

**Not in calibration-tests:** per-model variants such as `bench/` or one-off experiments. Add those only under `models/{model_slug}/`.

## Promote / demote

- **Promote:** add `{variant}/server.yaml` and `client.yaml` under `calibration-tests/`, then register the variant in `tester-v1/src/calibration.py` (today hardcoded to the three names above). Do not copy probe YAML into live model dirs; see `calibration-tests-sync.mdc`.
- **Demote:** remove from `calibration-tests/` only; live copies may stay.

**Default edits:** change shared behavior in `calibration-tests/`. One-off tweaks stay in that model's variant dir and are not copied to `calibration-tests/` unless promoted.

When `calibration-tests/` changes, follow `calibration-tests-sync.mdc`.

## How calibration uses calibration-tests

`tester_v1_calibrate.py` validates `calibration-tests/{variant}/`, then runs probes in-process with:

- probe server/client from `calibration-tests/{variant}/`
- ephemeral result layout under `models/{model}/{variant}/` (parent supplies `model.yaml`)

## Do not run on calibration-tests

Never pass `tester-v1/calibration-tests/` (or a variant under it) to `tester_v1_run_test.py`. Run test requires a model variant dir such as `models/{slug}/bench/`.
